        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c96180f4727b4ef4b8590002493046e2",
      "statement": "On a filename collision within the destination date folder, process_image appends numeric suffixes _1, _2, ... as {name}_{counter}{ext} via a while os.path.exists(new_file_path) loop and logs 'Filename collision detected for <base_name>, using <new_name>' at info level; colliding files are additive, never overwrites.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sortinfolder.py#L184-L193",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:87ffde225cecd5c869d68eac3c6684275392c74521a7dd37a65620154153ab9a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_749b61737b054d97a24b98507ae11e80",
      "statement": "In a real run process_image copies first with shutil.copy2, then rotates the copy with rotate_image_according_to_exif(new_file_path), then tags the copy with add_relative_path_tag(new_file_path, relative_path) — all mutation targets new_file_path, never the source file.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sortinfolder.py#L215-L221",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6312790a2efd7f66a083119e90306dfd8798aaa6ab63520e4b4e9061d9a7e5a7:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_73b8701d1ab048ed94229cc0c57de569",
      "statement": "Rotation is applied to the copied destination file, not the original: rotate_image_according_to_exif is called on new_file_path and re-saves in place only for EXIF Orientation values 3, 6, or 8 (180, 270, 90 degrees respectively); other or missing values leave the copy untouched and the source's orientation tag is never rewritten.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sortinfolder.py#L218-L218",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:270b059cee177ae3c1ebddd91edcbd0bd266179289b051159c1a0f79c435e792:"
